.TH focusforge-cli-retouch 1  "retouch 0.1.0-rc.1" 
.SH NAME
focusforge\-cli\-retouch \- Append an op list to a project as new states, one per op, each the previous one\*(Aqs child: on the current head, or on `\-\-from` as a branch. `export \-\-checkpoint` writes any of them
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfocusforge\-cli retouch\fR [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-ops\fR> <\fIPROJECT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Append an op list to a project as new states, one per op, each the previous one\*(Aqs child: on the current head, or on `\-\-from` as a branch. `export \-\-checkpoint` writes any of them
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ops\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
The op list: a JSON array of ops in the persisted `Op` shape. A brush stroke blends frame `source_id` over the image along its path: fully within `radius * (1 \- softness)`, fading linearly to nothing at `radius`. Every op is checked before anything is written; positions in error messages count from 0 in list order
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
The state to append under \-\- any unique prefix of its id. Defaults to the project\*(Aqs current head
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name the last appended state
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the JSON report instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Increase log detail (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Log errors only
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to append to
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0-rc.1
